{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChDFVBwM7WHmWoXi67X1g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I judged `vmci_resource_remove` in `samples/s207.c` not vulnerable and wrote that to `results/s207.json` (`is_vulnerable: false`, no CWE, no vulnerable statements).\n\nWhy:\n- **Correct match:** while holding the table lock, it looks for the entry by both its handle and its resource type. So it can't remove a different resource that happens to share the same handle.\n- **Safe for lock-free readers:** it unlinks the entry with `hlist_del_init_rcu`, releases the lock, then calls `synchronize_rcu()`. Any code still reading the table without the lock finishes before the reference is dropped.\n- **No early free:** it drops its own reference with `vmci_resource_put()`, then waits on `resource->done`. The caller can't free the object until every other holder has released it.\n\nAs far as I can tell this is the fixed form of the code. If an earlier version matched only on the handle, that one could remove the wrong resource; this one checks the type as well. I checked only this one file, as instructed, so I couldn't confirm how the helpers it calls behave."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":962,"cache_read_input_tokens":22190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":962},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05ea985b-fd50-4d52-9fc6-1827797abc03","uuid":"232aeec0-d40d-4c6b-b222-c11ad8c33c7e","timestamp":"2026-11-20T00:41:30.302Z","request_id":"req_011ChDFVBnRDPrUUvN5u3J96"}
